---
import RaceLayout from '../layouts/RaceLayout.astro';
import Garage from '../components/garage/Garage.astro';
import ControlsTables from '../components/garage/ControlsTables.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import { BINDING, SOURCE, STATUS, TESTED_CONTROLLERS, type Status } from '../lib/controls';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<RaceLayout
	title="Garage: ReCarbon controls"
	description="ReCarbon's keyboard and controller controls, interactive: driving, menus and the Settings overlay, with how each one was verified."
>
	<section class="section garage-page">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Garage · Controls</p>
			<h1 class="display title">Tune your controls</h1>
			<p class="intro">
				ReCarbon turns the keyboard into an Xbox 360 controller. Pick a device and a mode; hover, tap or tab
				through the list to light up each control. These are the <strong>defaults</strong>: you can rebind every key.
			</p>

			<Garage />

			<div class="panels">
				<details class="panel cut">
					<summary>Text table: every mode</summary>
					<ControlsTables />
				</details>

				<details class="panel cut" id="your-bindings">
					<summary>Your bindings</summary>
					<p>
						The Garage shows ReCarbon's defaults. To change a key, open Settings (<kbd>F1</kbd>, <kbd>Fn</kbd>+<kbd
							>F1</kbd
						> or <kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>,</kbd>), go to <strong>Controls</strong> with <kbd>Q</kbd> / <kbd>E</kbd>, pick a row
						and press <kbd>Space</kbd>, then the new key. <kbd>⌫</kbd> clears a slot; <kbd>⌦</kbd> resets the control.
					</p>
					<p>Or edit the <code>[keys]</code> table of <code>~/Library/Application Support/ReCarbon/settings.toml</code>:</p>
					<pre><code>[keys]
right_trigger = "w"
right_trigger_2 = "up"      # a second key for the same control
left_stick_left = "a"
left_stick_left_2 = "left"
x = "left_shift"</code></pre>
					<p>
						Names are physical key positions (<code>"semicolon"</code>, <code>"keypad_1"</code>, <code>"none"</code>).
						Keyboard and controller profiles and WASD / Arrows presets are <strong>planned (M8)</strong>.
						<a href={url('docs/controls/#rebinding-keys')}>More on rebinding</a>
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="panel cut">
					<summary>Controller notes</summary>
					<p>
						<StatusBadge status={BINDING.physicalController.status} /> No physical controller has been hand-tested with ReCarbon yet.
						The mapping below is pinned by a unit test; what each button does in a race is still to verify.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							ReCarbon reads pads through SDL3 by button position: South, East, West, North are A, B, X, Y. On a
							PlayStation-style pad that makes Cross A, Circle B, Square X and Triangle Y; the Xbox / PlayStation switch
							above changes the names shown, not the mapping. No PlayStation controller has been tested.
						</li>
						<li>
							The bumpers, triggers, sticks, stick presses, View, Menu and D-pad map one to one.
						</li>
						<li>
							<StatusBadge status="not-mapped" /> Back paddles, extra buttons and the Guide button aren't read by ReCarbon.
							If a pad's own firmware or software remaps a paddle to another button, it acts as that button: ReCarbon only
							sees the result.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</details>

				<section class="panel cut" aria-labelledby="tested-title">
					<h2 id="tested-title">Tested controllers</h2>
					{
						TESTED_CONTROLLERS.length ? (
							<ul>
								{TESTED_CONTROLLERS.map((t) => (
									<li>
										<strong>{t.model}</strong>: hand-tested {t.date}. {t.evidence}
									</li>
								))}
							</ul>
						) : (
							<p>
								None yet. A controller model is listed here only after it passes a physical hand test with ReCarbon (the
								first is due in milestone M5). A listing records a test result; it is not an endorsement or a
								recommendation.
							</p>
						)
					}
				</section>

				<section class="panel cut legend" aria-labelledby="legend-title">
					<h2 id="legend-title">Status legend</h2>
					<ul>
						{
							(Object.keys(STATUS) as Status[]).map((s) => (
								<li>
									<StatusBadge status={s} /> <span>{STATUS[s].meaning}</span>
								</li>
							))
						}
					</ul>
					<p class="src">
						Generated from ReCarbon's source{SOURCE.commit && <> at <code>{SOURCE.commit.slice(0, 7)}</code></>}:
						{SOURCE.files.map((f, i) => (
							<>
								{i > 0 && ', '}
								<code>{f}</code>
							</>
						))}.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</RaceLayout>

<style>
	.title {
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
		color: #c3cad6;
	}
	.panels {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}
	.panel {
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--rn-carbon);
		border: 1px solid var(--rn-graphite);
	}
	.panel summary {
		min-height: 44px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		font-family: var(--rn-font-display);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.panel h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-family: var(--rn-font-display);
		font-size: 1rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.panel :global(kbd) {
		font-family: var(--rn-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8em;
		padding: 0 0.35em;
		border: 1px solid #3a4250;
		border-bottom-width: 2px;
		border-radius: 3px;
	}
	.panel pre {
		overflow-x: auto;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		background: #0b0d10;
		border: 1px solid var(--rn-graphite);
		font-family: var(--rn-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.panel code {
		font-family: var(--rn-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85em;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.legend ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.legend li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: baseline;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.src {
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--rn-muted);
	}
</style>
